        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": "h3",
          "id": "",
          "text": "Important: Don't ignore early warning signs"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Camshaft issues can quickly escalate into serious engine damage, leading to significantly higher repair costs. If you notice unusual noises, loss of power or warning lights, get your vehicle diagnosed by a qualified specialist as soon as possible. On interference engines, a cam/crank correlation code (P0016-P0019) is an emergency. If timing is off enough, pistons will hit valves. Don't clear the code and hope - diagnose immediately. A £400-£900 camshaft replacement now saves a £2,500-£6,500 engine replacement later."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Symptom to cost - escalation"
        }
